      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:1:3:8:2",
      "relations": {
        "Mentions": [
          "/books/quran:53:42"
        ]
      },
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ يَقُولُ وَ أَنَّ إِلى رَبِّكَ الْمُنْتَهى فَإِذَا انْتَهَى الْكَلَامُ إِلَى اللَّهِ فَأَمْسِكُوا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Abdul Rahman Bin Al Hajjal, from Suleyman Bin Khalid who said, ",
          "‘Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Allah<sup>azwj</sup> Mighty and Majestic is Saying <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:53#h42\"><a href=\"/books/quran:53#h42\">[53:42]</a></a> And that to your Lord is the ending</span>. so when the speech (discussion) ends up to Allah<sup>azwj</sup> (His<sup>azwj</sup> Essence), so hold (stop there and refrain from further comments)’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          " 2. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad from ibn abu ‘Umayr from ’Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Hajjaj from Sulayman ibn Khalid from Imam abu ‘Abdallah (a.s.), who has said the following. “The words of Allah, the Majestic, the Glorious, that say, ‘And that the final end is unto thy Lord.” <a href=\"/#/books/quran:53#h42\"><a href=\"/books/quran:53#h42\">[53:42]</a></a> instructs people to end a discussion that would take up Allah’s self as an object of investigation.”"
        ]
      }
    },
